        "name": "RITU MATHUR",
        "role": "Former Director - Confederation of Indian Industry (CII) Head - National Foundation for Corporate Governance (NFCG)",
        "bio": "Ritu Mathur is a seasoned governance and technology leader with 35 years of experience spanning corporate governance, public policy, regulatory strategy, gender diversity, and leadership transformation. As Former Director of the Confederation of Indian Industry and Head of the National Foundation for Corporate Governance, she has designed the standards by which Indian industries lead and govern themselves.\n\nHer influence reaches well beyond national borders. Through her contributions to the B20 ESG Action Council and the G20 Anti-Corruption Working Group, she has championed integrity, sustainability, and ethical leadership on some of the world's most consequential platforms. Her senior leadership tenure as Chief Regulatory at Tata Teleservices Limited further shaped her as a leader who bridges strategic vision with techno-regulatory expertise.\n\nEqually committed to India's cultural identity, Ritu is the author of a pioneering coffee table book on Ancient Indian Wisdom through Calligraphy, a work UNESCO recognized as a significant contribution to documenting India's written heritage. She was also celebrated in Sheroes Amongst Us for her inspiring journey of resilience, purpose, and leadership grace.\n\nThrough her initiative Chrysalis Sutra, she now focuses on developing emotionally intelligent, purpose-driven women leaders who are equipped not just to navigate systems, but to transform them.\n\nAt TEDxBistupur 2026, Ritu will invite the audience to ask why our oldest wisdom traditions still hold the most honest answers to our newest leadership challenges and why the women leading tomorrow must be rooted in identity and inner clarity, not just capability.",
